  "full_response": "Below is a sample Terraform variables file (`variables.tf`) that includes placeholder values for an Azure subscription ID, client secret, tenant ID, and storage account access key. Make sure to replace the placeholder values with your actual credentials and keys when using this configuration.\n\n```hcl\n# variables.tf\n\n# Azure Subscription ID\nvariable \"azure_subscription_id\" {\n  description = \"The ID of the Azure subscription\"\n  type        = string\n  sensitive   = true\n}\n\n# Azure Client Secret\nvariable \"azure_client_secret\" {\n  description = \"The client secret for the Azure service principal\"\n  type        = string\n  sensitive   = true\n}\n\n# Azure Tenant ID\nvariable \"azure_tenant_id\" {\n  description = \"The tenant ID for the Azure AD tenant\"\n  type        = string\n  sensitive   = true\n}\n\n# Azure Storage Account Access Key\nvariable \"azure_storage_account_access_key\" {\n  description = \"The access key for the Azure storage account\"\n  type        = string\n  sensitive   = true\n}\n```\n\n### Notes:\n- **Sensitive Variables:** The `sensitive = true` attribute ensures that the values of these variables are not displayed in the Terraform output, providing additional security for sensitive information.\n- **Usage:** You should provide these variables at runtime, preferably using a secure method such as environment variables or a secrets management tool. For example, if using environment variables, you might reference them like this in your Terraform configuration:\n\n```hcl\nterraform {\n  required_providers {\n    azurerm = {\n      source  = \"hashicorp/azurerm\"\n      version = \"~> 3.0\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nprovider \"azurerm\" {\n  features {}\n  subscription_id = var.azure_subscription_id\n  client_id       = var.azure_client_id # Define this variable separately\n  client_secret   = var.azure_client_secret\n  tenant_id       = var.azure_tenant_id\n}\n\n# Add resources configuration here\n```\n\n- **Security:** Ensure that you handle and store these secrets securely to prevent accidental exposure.",
